/**
 * The partitioning contract for scan-rooted kernels (plan:
 * plans/lmdb-native-engine/32-parallel-kernel-parity-closure.md, M3).
 *
 * <p>
 * The interpreted parallel engine range-partitions any root pattern scan, while the kernel rungs could only partition
 * an adjacency or domain root — so a kernel lowered onto a raw scan lost its parallelism for that reason alone. The fix
 * hands each worker's {@link LmdbNativeKernelScanner} one planned {@link LmdbRootScanPartition}, which is the
 * scan-rooted counterpart of the adjacency rungs' key window.
 *
 * <p>
 * The property that has to hold before any of that is safe is the one asserted here: the partitions form an exact
 * partition of the full scan. Not a cover (which would duplicate rows) and not a subset (which would drop them) — every
 * quad exactly once.
 */
